    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7323" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĕleusma</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĕleuma</span></b> ),
		ătis, n. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĕleusma</span></b> , ae,
		f., Ven. Vita S. <i><span class="en">Mart. 4, 423</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλευσμα ʽκέλευμα</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a command</i> or <i>call given by
				the chief oarsman</i>, <i>which gave the time to
				the rowers</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 67, 4</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Rutil. 1, 370</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Ascon. Cic. Div. in Caecil. 17,
		55</span></i>.</div>
